<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys April full range naphtha above $230/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys April full range naphtha above $230/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought by tender 30,000 tonnes of full range naphtha for April 1-20 delivery at just above $230.00 per tonne on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Kaohsiung, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender closed March 10 and was valid until March 12.</p>
<p>The award was lower than CPC's last full range naphtha award at $239-$240 per tonne c-and-f March 11-20 delivery.</p>
<p>The official said the next CPC naphtha tender would be for May imports of naphthenic-and-aromatic (N+A) naphtha.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
